WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.570
A data centre.

2
00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:04.850
Rack after rack of spinning hard disks.

3
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:10.750
One online backup company tracked over
300,000 hard drives in its data centres.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.130
But many new laptops use an SSD instead.

5
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.910
So why stick with spinning disks there?

6
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.930
Are hard disks just faster for big files?

7
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.250
In this mission, you'll see how secondary
storage keeps your files when the power

8
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.190
is off.

9
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:30.350
You'll look inside a hard disk: spinning
platters and a moving read write head.

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.510
And inside an SSD,
built from flash memory,

11
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.350
with no moving parts.

12
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.490
Then you'll weigh them up
on capacity, speed and cost.

13
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:45.200
Your mission: decide why a firm storing
that much data chooses spinning hard disks.
